# Failure ladder

Every external call through `app/gateway/**` (LiteLLM model aliases) and
`app/providers/**` (video generation providers) must follow this ladder in order.
Do not skip rungs or reorder them. Provider capability negotiation stays in
`.cursor/rules/14-provider-abstraction-mcp.mdc` — this rule covers resilience only.

## Rung 1 — Retry

- Exponential backoff with jitter.
- Retryable errors only (transient HTTP 5xx, timeouts, rate limits).
- Max **3** attempts per call.

## Rung 2 — Fallback

- Switch to an alternate model or provider **within the same alias / capability group**.
- Never fall back to a different alias without explicit config.

## Rung 3 — Circuit break

- Per dependency (gateway alias or provider id).
- Opens after **5 failures in 30 seconds**.
- Half-open probe before closing.

## Rung 4 — Degrade

- Return cached, stale, or partial result when available.
- Always flag the response as degraded (`PARTIAL` or equivalent metadata).
- Never silently pass degraded output as fully successful.

## Rung 5 — Fail honestly

- Raise a typed `AppError` with a **stable error code**.
- Message states what failed, what was preserved, and what to do next.
- Every error response carries the run's **`trace_id`**.

## Scope

| Path | Applies |
|---|---|
| `app/gateway/**` | All LiteLLM proxy calls (logical aliases only — never provider names in code) |
| `app/providers/**` | All video-generation provider calls behind the abstraction |

Folder-scoped rules (`10`–`18`) do not cover the gateway folder; this always-applied
rule fills that gap so model-call resilience is never missed.
